ole": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "1017 never contacts 1593 directly (step_15), and 1017's out-neighborhood is disjoint from 1593's in-neighborhood (step_03/step_04/step_16), so no 2-hop relay exists. Expanding nine of 1017's out-neighbors (steps 06-14) produced no second-hop node that is 1593 or feeds 1593. 1593 sits in a tight, self-contained 24-node cluster. Because time-ignoring reachability is necessary for a time-respecting cascade, the 600-unit-gap chain cannot exist in [42136, 80535]. High overall event volume (step_01) and hub 1704's popularity (step_10) were checked as alternative explanations and do not create any route; the low repeat ratio and one-event-per-partner profile of both endpoints (step_02) further argue against a relay channel. Confidence is held below certainty because a minority of 1017's out-neighbors were not individually expanded."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structural prerequisites for a cascade 1017 \u2192 1593:**\n\n- Both nodes are low-activity, purely \"fan-out\"/\"fan-in\" style nodes: 1017 has 25 events / 25 distinct partners, 1593 has 23 events / 23 partners (step_02) \u2014 every interaction is a distinct edge, so there is no repeated-contact channel that would make tightly-spaced relay plausible.\n- **No direct edge:** 0 events in either direction between 1017 and 1593 over the entire horizon (step_15). So any cascade needs \u22652 relay hops, each within 600 time units.\n- **No 1-hop overlap:** 1017's out-neighbors {25, 65, 160, 180, 270, 271, 388, 401, 531, 851, 949, 1237, 1281, 1314, 1323, 1380, 1704, 1713, 1716, 1738, 1866} (step_03) are disjoint from 1593's in-neighbors {26, 64, 478, 502, 603, 706, 830, 873, 961, 971, 1000, 1215, 1325, 1477, 1529, 1622, 1631, 1870, 1916, 1940} (step_04, step_16).\n- **No 2-hop path found:** expanding nine of 1017's out-neighbors \u2014 25 (step_06), 65 (step_07), 949 (step_08), 1237 (step_09), 1704 (step_10), 160 (step_11), 270 (step_12), 401 (step_13), 851 (step_14) \u2014 yields 71 second-hop targets, none of which is 1593 or any in-neighbor of 1593. 1593's neighborhood (step_16) is a tight, self-contained cluster of 24 nodes with no contact from the 1017 side.\n\n**Confounder controls:** the graph is large and busy (16,085 events, 15,217 distinct edges, repeat_ratio 0.054 \u2014 step_01), and 1704 is a locally popular hub with 26 out-partners (step_10). That ambient volume and hub popularity could superficially suggest reachability, but neither produces any path into 1593's neighborhood, let alone one respecting the 600-unit inter-event budget across the 38,399-unit query window.\n\n**Conclusion:** the shortest 1017\u21921593 route is \u22653 hops and no candidate relay chain was found even when time is ignored. Since time-ignoring reachability is a necessary condition for a time-respecting cascade, the cascade cannot be supported.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_bd1bd500\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1017, 1593],\n  \"window\": [42136, 80535],\n  \"confidence\": 0.63,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1017 never contacts 1593 directly (step_15), and 1017's out-neighborhood is disjoint from 1593's in-neighborhood (step_03/step_04/step_16), so no 2-hop relay exists. Expanding nine of 1017's out-neighbors (steps 06-14) produced no second-hop node that is 1593 or feeds 1593. 1593 sits in a tight, self-contained 24-node cluster. Because time-ignoring reachability is necessary for a time-respecting cascade, the 600-unit-gap chain cannot exist in [42136, 80535]. High overall event volume (step_01) and hub 1704's popularity (step_10) were checked as alternative explanations and do not create any route; the low repeat ratio and one-event-per-partner profile of both endpoints (step_02) further argue against a relay channel. Confidence is held below certainty because a minority of 1017's out-neighbors were not individually expanded.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 31001, "total_output_tokens": 8618, "total_tokens": 39619, "total_latency_ms": 120658, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}